[{:db/id "q-132112/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "c392cd6f-3a69-576d-8921-68c0b89cf493" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0c8faefe-90c9-5934-b966-486bebae13b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "8acf5ca8-33a5-5bab-87f9-f27c9d61f55a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "bfb96d4f-007e-5edf-9407-ba107ff8fcd3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "06ef2e42-e66d-5c57-908d-d5d361e54c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f3a5335-82b9-5638-9237-d171488e70e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132112/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-132112/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-132112/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-132112/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-132112/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132112/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132112" :question/id #uuid "737247d2-cfc0-5a76-b6fc-cde80c2d39de" :question/math-academy-id "q-132112" :question/problem "Find the radius of curvature for the curve $r(t)$ at the point $r(\\pi )$ if the curve and the derivative ${T}^{′}(t)$ of the corresponding unit tangent vector are given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,4,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the curve $r(t)$ and the derivative ${T}^{′}(t)$ of the unit tangent, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(\\pi ),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${T}^{′}(\\pi )$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the radius of curvature at $r(\\pi )$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖}{‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132112/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d622a24-2705-53bb-a07f-8cc11775cf09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132112"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection/36bd4767b4dcb6cbfe49e6bf46e014bd92e359a1fadf3fe464658fcbf70d048e" :answer/id #uuid "d3034a6e-67ed-5c41-9817-d96de6cb8d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" :answer/id #uuid "d8c69805-a374-5f80-aeb7-953618d64989" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "a048a76f-88b6-5380-8828-7a623150cbd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "2d2b9eb9-7d2a-5d23-aacc-4f60dffa1d9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285" :answer/id #uuid "b367ab11-08ab-5645-8aba-60737936b8ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "941a71bf-a7f5-5dc4-941d-2574a5f7c29d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64738/selection/36bd4767b4dcb6cbfe49e6bf46e014bd92e359a1fadf3fe464658fcbf70d048e" :answer-field/choices ["q-64738/selection/36bd4767b4dcb6cbfe49e6bf46e014bd92e359a1fadf3fe464658fcbf70d048e" "q-64738/selection/b05ae51c7e0f9ce8edef362b0e3bfd104c905bad9c2676254ee36131cb916baa" "q-64738/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-64738/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-64738/selection/b937b5a9c9148a5914243385a1d84bacb019d6c5ff771ce01182a0f3091b9285"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64738" :question/id #uuid "10c6bbff-8da1-5a79-9fe0-55dfb246fa04" :question/math-academy-id "q-64738" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that  its  unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature: \n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,-\\frac{4}{5}(-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{8}{25}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,\\frac{8}{25}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{25}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{8}{25}\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}))}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{25}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})+{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{8}{25})}=\\frac{25}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d622a24-2705-53bb-a07f-8cc11775cf09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "5d8439ce-189c-5040-9908-63da18191d18" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "6ca36da4-9c28-56c8-997f-bf786abee190" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a9c7d34b-c25a-5428-8ee0-c1959cae06f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "a05e3edb-7e8e-57ba-a448-beece5846792" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "adcf0a33-58ff-5c6f-9db0-2338f29becfc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc1494de-5bd4-5937-8164-8ebbc73c4adb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132105/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-132105/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-132105/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-132105/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-132105/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-132105/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132105" :question/id #uuid "2282cba5-0247-5d06-9d27-a008f1535719" :question/math-academy-id "q-132105" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}+{(-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡s+{cos}^{2}⁡s+2{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2{cos}^{2}⁡s+2{sin}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2({cos}^{2}⁡s+{sin}^{2}⁡s)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{1}=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-132105/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d622a24-2705-53bb-a07f-8cc11775cf09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132105"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection/f4a9310cbaa6584a30e8ae8e9d3f2fa9d369bb63353966e97a97e3685abfbe09" :answer/id #uuid "d3686bab-c21e-5d91-81b8-c6319f40a50e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{s}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection/c9c77a3b4e3132de64b63abb2df1d725fb0044f8e4ecae5d545cd827cc9e9fce" :answer/id #uuid "ccf9b47e-e00f-5d5c-a01d-7d5038cffb59" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{s}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection/2e458dad81b93f0c5b3923bf58859b89de8c6b5b0619e48c170517cdb4ffa49e" :answer/id #uuid "d03bb83c-ae8b-5801-9a64-9ebcffe18262" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{s}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection/394c78cf5e1699a59f8c4fa5961966cccf3bea18da9362cf4d374743b9bf65e2" :answer/id #uuid "27412797-7dea-54d7-88c5-e908ae84a43f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2s" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection/540d764cdc22c13bf73253c5a3f923cfef50e0211ce5428646723cc221b67ad6" :answer/id #uuid "6ca16f3b-45d5-594b-ac3d-671bfaf67656" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6526d23b-95c2-55cd-b8e7-c5f6943b2643" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132110/selection/c9c77a3b4e3132de64b63abb2df1d725fb0044f8e4ecae5d545cd827cc9e9fce" :answer-field/choices ["q-132110/selection/f4a9310cbaa6584a30e8ae8e9d3f2fa9d369bb63353966e97a97e3685abfbe09" "q-132110/selection/c9c77a3b4e3132de64b63abb2df1d725fb0044f8e4ecae5d545cd827cc9e9fce" "q-132110/selection/2e458dad81b93f0c5b3923bf58859b89de8c6b5b0619e48c170517cdb4ffa49e" "q-132110/selection/394c78cf5e1699a59f8c4fa5961966cccf3bea18da9362cf4d374743b9bf65e2" "q-132110/selection/540d764cdc22c13bf73253c5a3f923cfef50e0211ce5428646723cc221b67ad6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132110" :question/id #uuid "41406066-0d4c-5ab4-ae88-9853e3376928" :question/math-academy-id "q-132110" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\sqrt{3}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\sqrt{3})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}}{2\\sqrt{s}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡\\sqrt{s}+{cos}^{2}⁡\\sqrt{s}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{s}})}=4\\sqrt{s}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-132110/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d622a24-2705-53bb-a07f-8cc11775cf09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132110"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "69ea459b-5aa4-5457-83b2-86e89add2c3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3cc57fcc-f5b4-5184-8590-7a01fda22ee0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer/id #uuid "ba0248a6-d752-51fe-9341-6ef9d1b98f2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "3fa44a25-bfcb-5e96-bfe9-e191bb7416f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "b7482c83-6e34-52c4-8e97-d128ce69ef73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8499c4a-b922-5211-8821-9193f113ea5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64732/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-64732/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-64732/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-64732/selection/07791849728418b50d59d705e3d959e93383e408886fd319ae3a513a1b7159ba" "q-64732/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-64732/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64732" :question/id #uuid "1a75f579-8ee0-5607-99e3-d5f80c6111fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-64732" :question/problem "Consider a curve $r(s)$ parametrized by its arc length $s.$ Find the radius of curvature of $r(s)$ at an arbitrary point knowing that  its  unit tangent vector $T(s)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\,k\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since the curve $r(s)$ and its unit tangent vector $T(s)$ are both parametrized by arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature: \n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{κ(s)}=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}\n$$\n\nWe differentiate $T(s)$ with respect to $s$ and calculate its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))\\,i+\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,i+\\frac{2}{9}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})\\,j] \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(s)‖ & =\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}))}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})+{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(s)=\\frac{1}{‖{T}^{′}(s)‖}=\\frac{1}{(\\frac{2}{9})}=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64732/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d622a24-2705-53bb-a07f-8cc11775cf09"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64732"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection/e399bdf70c848a8c809c9b5d18b52f0659081361ea94caf84c581b9c3cd2fc2a" :answer/id #uuid "87be91eb-8b6a-5a21-8299-877e02225dfa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{10}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection/31bf78361df244e9fc9450338db55b4d9a63afb40f1a493b00ee3ccc8b456084" :answer/id #uuid "debccc52-f963-5379-8b1a-86b31580c2b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection/c05362aeb9b03871f6738b897095fe63f5727d236a52361355cb7032df7cc80f" :answer/id #uuid "4f5756c2-5310-5d5c-92d9-53a20fc16dca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(1,0)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection/c92424ab79fd2c401bd6e062b54069350fd74569c20e280a41aa85af060729d9" :answer/id #uuid "8e5b10e5-7637-5c34-8764-fe163edd2055" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(1,1)$ and the radius is $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection/a93d2f3d62e22b158663b2888ed4ea96506c50c6f53142246740b616350193b7" :answer/id #uuid "7fff7941-c4b3-5e8c-b317-f97d6b4ed220" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1c3146c-10db-5d80-af47-1c972475df55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64836/selection/31bf78361df244e9fc9450338db55b4d9a63afb40f1a493b00ee3ccc8b456084" :answer-field/choices ["q-64836/selection/e399bdf70c848a8c809c9b5d18b52f0659081361ea94caf84c581b9c3cd2fc2a" "q-64836/selection/31bf78361df244e9fc9450338db55b4d9a63afb40f1a493b00ee3ccc8b456084" "q-64836/selection/c05362aeb9b03871f6738b897095fe63f5727d236a52361355cb7032df7cc80f" "q-64836/selection/c92424ab79fd2c401bd6e062b54069350fd74569c20e280a41aa85af060729d9" "q-64836/selection/a93d2f3d62e22b158663b2888ed4ea96506c50c6f53142246740b616350193b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64836" :question/id #uuid "42a574c4-fd0d-57cc-b972-6174b753f17e" :question/math-academy-id "q-64836" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(3,1)$ where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, given that $‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖=2,$ and the unit tangent vector to the curve is $\\,T(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=⟨3,1⟩,$ since the point $P(3,1)$ is at the tip of $r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})$ and $‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=⟨-1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖ & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=\\frac{2}{1}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{‖{T}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})‖}=⟨-1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+R(\\frac{\\pi }{2})N(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨3,1⟩+2⟨-1,0⟩=⟨1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64836/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64836"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection/60da13694ac6129bcdebfa14623c090f7ac20d713fc29798798d64359ec3f970" :answer/id #uuid "84df81f6-3e54-528a-b6cf-3992562b10c9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(\\pi ,1)$ and the radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection/973f28d50c4b2d274680d48d0fe670bde432c3fe0d441d4b1eba0a0490c1a6b4" :answer/id #uuid "0ca2262b-4b0f-5dc8-88da-1dec59056be6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(\\pi ,-1)$ and the radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection/99d851527b2e5837b834ebba816b54d0b26e373b0b611c15ac6cd1adbb5d6e3d" :answer/id #uuid "b4447a5c-768f-5647-822c-5d2c8bb84083" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(\\pi ,-2)$ and the radius $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection/e67ad6ca993fe1075231c9a41604fe1aefc71e53f4a543859c2dad2fa95db6dd" :answer/id #uuid "95ff2f36-ecd7-510b-834d-383e6b07f3e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(\\pi ,0)$ and the radius $\\frac{1}{4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection/b0a78e543658c196c658f08fb0f5b3dddfc60c60227d82db396b886be700ce88" :answer/id #uuid "3f78124d-52d5-5972-b00c-001c137051cc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(\\pi ,0)$ and the radius $4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea1c74ac-36bf-510b-bebb-39ebcfb0f08f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97594/selection/99d851527b2e5837b834ebba816b54d0b26e373b0b611c15ac6cd1adbb5d6e3d" :answer-field/choices ["q-97594/selection/60da13694ac6129bcdebfa14623c090f7ac20d713fc29798798d64359ec3f970" "q-97594/selection/973f28d50c4b2d274680d48d0fe670bde432c3fe0d441d4b1eba0a0490c1a6b4" "q-97594/selection/99d851527b2e5837b834ebba816b54d0b26e373b0b611c15ac6cd1adbb5d6e3d" "q-97594/selection/e67ad6ca993fe1075231c9a41604fe1aefc71e53f4a543859c2dad2fa95db6dd" "q-97594/selection/b0a78e543658c196c658f08fb0f5b3dddfc60c60227d82db396b886be700ce88"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97594" :question/id #uuid "7b6d4e9d-2bd2-557f-873b-90eaa73125fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-97594" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(\\pi ,2)$ where $t=\\pi $, given that $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖=2,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(\\pi )=⟨\\pi ,2⟩$,  since the point $P(\\pi ,2)$ is at the tip of $r(\\pi ).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t),$ ${T}^{′}(\\pi )$ and $‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{t}{2}),-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{t}{2})⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})⟩=\\frac{1}{2}⟨0,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖}{‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖}=\\frac{2}{(\\frac{1}{2})}=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=\\pi $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(\\pi ) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(\\pi )}{‖{T}^{′}(\\pi )‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{(\\frac{1}{2})}⟨0,-1⟩=⟨0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\pi )+R(\\pi )N(\\pi ) & =⟨\\pi ,2⟩+4⟨0,-1⟩=⟨\\pi ,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97594/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97594"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection/0b2a94511ff644c6490be4618387a359fd6738f4e1406fc599298f4f042eb66f" :answer/id #uuid "06e0ac57-73d2-51a7-8942-2aaf5928ed9d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection/6de0fa7e7cc280b57c3346a7061525815a2b09bfe19d11a3ad019acc5b7b812d" :answer/id #uuid "40c96597-5f0b-542b-80bc-7c3a19beb22d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨0,-1⟩$ and the radius is $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection/255f643e571202f3c068483b7cca7a369b156af1be100aa2ce2df93c5457a17d" :answer/id #uuid "931a23c3-fdf4-53a3-916e-f1762a47c587" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,1⟩$ and the radius is $1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection/3c18b98051ff4dbe59d7e0717ec47ed1b95236e8534cff71e17a8e08aef818be" :answer/id #uuid "cc50ba91-6f74-5966-ac6a-42ad2c634fae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,0⟩$ and the radius is $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection/edfe935b494b64ed928bb92297fa81440562f3850fac04391d05bb4bb4fd2d40" :answer/id #uuid "cd975c9e-348d-546c-b2f4-1d8da0b57a95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,-1⟩$ and the radius is $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "adf9c8f9-d885-56ea-ab9d-feb7e51adfbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132204/selection/0b2a94511ff644c6490be4618387a359fd6738f4e1406fc599298f4f042eb66f" :answer-field/choices ["q-132204/selection/0b2a94511ff644c6490be4618387a359fd6738f4e1406fc599298f4f042eb66f" "q-132204/selection/6de0fa7e7cc280b57c3346a7061525815a2b09bfe19d11a3ad019acc5b7b812d" "q-132204/selection/255f643e571202f3c068483b7cca7a369b156af1be100aa2ce2df93c5457a17d" "q-132204/selection/3c18b98051ff4dbe59d7e0717ec47ed1b95236e8534cff71e17a8e08aef818be" "q-132204/selection/edfe935b494b64ed928bb92297fa81440562f3850fac04391d05bb4bb4fd2d40"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132204" :question/id #uuid "3e19d212-99bc-5ec6-ba7f-76b0f4f4e8f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-132204" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(0,0)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=1,$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨0,0⟩,$ since the point $P(0,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨0,0⟩+1\\cdot ⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0⟩+⟨1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132204/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132204"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection/e49d86aa60b61f606fcf49f6c1639bd7e40b593ebcb1b82e3e9b9d89754336b2" :answer/id #uuid "68e1b396-4504-52b0-99a9-854348ff9b2a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection/a22b437fdcd031579a5bac8cf6f2a2fd1f437de46b279e227dcd4de182eff507" :answer/id #uuid "f5f00530-abf1-5f6f-a023-69f58f64c6f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,1)$ and the radius $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection/918647b48b45a6b438c52043305cc803df7bd5b25929f09ef4d3028d39c2b7f4" :answer/id #uuid "cfe4e281-53a3-5f83-abad-8611b20d89b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection/3028999e447597d3e02b9b9cf0c8dabeb08d43f662c729b760294ab4eee061b9" :answer/id #uuid "f2a1b7b9-a5a1-512d-a5e6-26a1b0c0fcf9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection/ff88b2e770ed59cf994a4bd1bb58c4785cb800a84f165ebd6be4d980c5b254fa" :answer/id #uuid "92a27b2b-9653-53ac-a288-bf4493224d4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $(0,-1)$ and the radius $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "823fcc0d-2b6a-5a5c-897f-b9188b5bb771" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97593/selection/e49d86aa60b61f606fcf49f6c1639bd7e40b593ebcb1b82e3e9b9d89754336b2" :answer-field/choices ["q-97593/selection/e49d86aa60b61f606fcf49f6c1639bd7e40b593ebcb1b82e3e9b9d89754336b2" "q-97593/selection/a22b437fdcd031579a5bac8cf6f2a2fd1f437de46b279e227dcd4de182eff507" "q-97593/selection/918647b48b45a6b438c52043305cc803df7bd5b25929f09ef4d3028d39c2b7f4" "q-97593/selection/3028999e447597d3e02b9b9cf0c8dabeb08d43f662c729b760294ab4eee061b9" "q-97593/selection/ff88b2e770ed59cf994a4bd1bb58c4785cb800a84f165ebd6be4d980c5b254fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97593" :question/id #uuid "4521979f-e782-519a-bada-dd0881c64439" :question/math-academy-id "q-97593" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(1,0)$ where $t=0$, given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=\\sqrt{2},$ and the unit tangent vector to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t),$ we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨1,0⟩,$ since the point $P(1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t),$ ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0⟩=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{1}=\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨1,0⟩+\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨-1,1⟩=⟨0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97593/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97593"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection/8a9f7415ef21374436c3f0eb4f22a60947ae91c140383668b5b9eb2d745975ba" :answer/id #uuid "ce4605b6-c47f-5a53-a750-f9bf49c9d12a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-1,2⟩$ and the radius is $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection/00746a7254910263a373703f6dac1b69994cafcbca64de728e9a84299af78466" :answer/id #uuid "788f4a87-bfc3-5976-b4f1-bb14205248cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨3,-2⟩$ and the radius is $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection/36dc2250fa7ef59a40a60129bc90e947eb1597f9ae9c5b96e10272968e1a2124" :answer/id #uuid "604da060-e8cc-532a-a513-c77ceffb3f64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-2,4⟩$ and the radius is $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection/0bd129ea52c3908d757284142121877cc20af4ccc381276a1c6c2c1e874994d8" :answer/id #uuid "057fc5ba-3762-57a9-bc66-3fcef26e1d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨-1,4⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection/e789ef859ce9479e82f5ec64f4ed26d9de7b1c0cdbbec6715c758826288220e2" :answer/id #uuid "d6123931-e82b-5a20-afd9-aa0bd8b3a4e5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The center is $⟨1,-2⟩$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b463491b-d65b-51ec-8dcc-461c6fdb8c60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132210/selection/00746a7254910263a373703f6dac1b69994cafcbca64de728e9a84299af78466" :answer-field/choices ["q-132210/selection/8a9f7415ef21374436c3f0eb4f22a60947ae91c140383668b5b9eb2d745975ba" "q-132210/selection/00746a7254910263a373703f6dac1b69994cafcbca64de728e9a84299af78466" "q-132210/selection/36dc2250fa7ef59a40a60129bc90e947eb1597f9ae9c5b96e10272968e1a2124" "q-132210/selection/0bd129ea52c3908d757284142121877cc20af4ccc381276a1c6c2c1e874994d8" "q-132210/selection/e789ef859ce9479e82f5ec64f4ed26d9de7b1c0cdbbec6715c758826288220e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132210" :question/id #uuid "917351e8-3e93-5c8c-b787-a39fdea6cdc6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132210" :question/problem "Find the center and radius of the osculating circle to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $P(1,0)$ where $t=0,$ given that $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖=\\sqrt{2},$ and the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ to the curve is\n\n$$\nT(t)=⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}},\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given both the value of $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖$ and the unit tangent $T(t)$, we will use the following formula for the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNotice that $r(0)=⟨1,0⟩,$ since the point $P(1,0)$ is at the tip of $r(0).$ \n\nNow, we find ${T}^{′}(t)$, ${T}^{′}(0)$ and $‖{T}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2t}+1}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{t}}{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{{e}^{2t}}{{({e}^{2t}+1)}^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\ {T}^{′}(0) & =⟨\\frac{{e}^{0}}{{({e}^{0}+1)}^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{{e}^{0}}{{({e}^{0}+1)}^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(0)‖ & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0)‖}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the principal normal vector at $t=0$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(0) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(0)}{‖{T}^{′}(0)‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of the osculating circle is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0)+R(0)N(0) & =⟨1,0⟩+2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩+2⟨1,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0⟩+⟨2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132210/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f6e70249-58d6-57ce-867c-ff9a3b4219f4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132210"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "5640273b-9b42-584b-819b-2150c4eb85c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "7c9301ba-d668-5d91-82ea-40d597a13d57" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "a99d331a-4459-5d43-8af7-df13ffd64339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "08d79041-205b-564e-8cb9-08efb1a51d19" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c46724a0-9e5b-5a1b-86d7-e0a90d011d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "83adfb6e-7423-5724-ac24-e55143fa15f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132128/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-132128/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-132128/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-132128/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" "q-132128/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-132128/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132128" :question/id #uuid "399b70b2-c26b-5787-bbea-067efe659b98" :question/math-academy-id "q-132128" :question/problem "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=0$ for the curve $r(t)=⟨4{t}^{2},\\,4t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given only the curve $r(t)$, we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$, ${r}^{′}(0),$ and $‖{r}^{′}(0)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8t,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(0) & =4⟨2(0),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)‖ & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =4⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =4⟨2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =8⟨1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(0) & =8⟨1,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(0)$ and ${r}^{″}(0)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0) & =4⟨0,\\,1,\\,0⟩\\times 8⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =32\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =32\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-32k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖ & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(0) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(0){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(0)\\times {r}^{″}(0)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{3}}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{32} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132128/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a053eb10-be16-5423-9b7b-c23677bb6335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132128"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection/34d68e4295f5536e87d3ea713ba3332fc6b9f89229b78e1ee04a33fb03f128bc" :answer/id #uuid "6bb767f0-57f5-5e48-badd-dc14414fb033" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection/32c91f7f799c73f67ac90b094d8e43e7b59fab5e2cea43af800dcb2690fbb807" :answer/id #uuid "d446cea7-8bb9-59f8-870a-6b25e344bebd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection/856fa93165758af3931888d5cf056d43eb99649f4205c206d9588977cc5a2491" :answer/id #uuid "2ccd1906-8c0e-58fb-8b13-29ecd27de00f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection/476d8b954cf781bd45a9d822e7afd9722074f8548a73c339a5307a53a16746e5" :answer/id #uuid "f07f8785-9418-58ed-b5d5-8456abd73ced" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection/d4cdb73eb4bce286f56c4b3e0a8b05862d4f6bb9d9eea3a1f57ba237919af600" :answer/id #uuid "4228ebe7-4faf-520a-8901-acb5b3fd5180" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "23a9c127-9716-543c-ba54-5120d2a3486c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-98668/selection/32c91f7f799c73f67ac90b094d8e43e7b59fab5e2cea43af800dcb2690fbb807" :answer-field/choices ["q-98668/selection/34d68e4295f5536e87d3ea713ba3332fc6b9f89229b78e1ee04a33fb03f128bc" "q-98668/selection/32c91f7f799c73f67ac90b094d8e43e7b59fab5e2cea43af800dcb2690fbb807" "q-98668/selection/856fa93165758af3931888d5cf056d43eb99649f4205c206d9588977cc5a2491" "q-98668/selection/476d8b954cf781bd45a9d822e7afd9722074f8548a73c339a5307a53a16746e5" "q-98668/selection/d4cdb73eb4bce286f56c4b3e0a8b05862d4f6bb9d9eea3a1f57ba237919af600"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-98668" :question/id #uuid "1ec30503-8a67-54c0-8a09-5a663e850850" :question/math-academy-id "q-98668" :question/problem "Find the radius of the osculating circle at the point where $t=\\pi $ for the curve $r(t)=⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Since we are given only the curve $r(t),$ we will use the cross product formula to find the radius of curvature:\n\n$$\nR(t)=\\frac{1}{κ(t)}=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t),$ ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and $‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ),\\,{e}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{e}^{\\pi },\\,-{e}^{\\pi }⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }⟨-1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )‖ & ={e}^{\\pi }\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{″}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=\\pi :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & =⟨-2{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi ,\\,2{e}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ⟩ \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi }⟨0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(\\pi )$ and ${r}^{″}(\\pi )$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi ) & ={e}^{\\pi }⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩\\times {e}^{\\pi }⟨0,\\,-2,\\,0⟩ \\\\  & ={({e}^{\\pi })}^{2}\\cdot \\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ \\,0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & ={e}^{2\\pi }\\cdot \\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ \\,0 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =2{e}^{2\\pi }\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖ & =2{e}^{2\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of curvature at $t=\\pi $ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(\\pi ) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi ){‖}^{3}}{‖{r}^{′}(\\pi )\\times {r}^{″}(\\pi )‖}=\\frac{{(\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi })}^{3}}{\\,2{e}^{2\\pi }\\,}=\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-98668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a053eb10-be16-5423-9b7b-c23677bb6335"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-98668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132130/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "976cd78e-05a7-5931-a573-c47f7eafbd1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132130/selection/d027d90726f5b